{"step_index":78,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T05:04:33Z","content":"I have built an interactive, peak-fidelity frontend for **AegisOS**: **The Ambient Mission Control & Spatial Actuator Simulator**.\n\nYou can open and experience the frontend directly:\n* **In-IDE Artifact**: [aegis_mission_control.html](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/brain/e426a91e-3961-4012-84ca-1849c4385ef7/aegis_mission_control.html)\n* **Local Project Code**: [`frontend/index.html`](file:///C:/Users/Piyush/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/aegis_os/frontend/index.html)\n\nTo launch it immediately in your default browser, run:\n```powershell\nstart C:\\Users\\Piyush\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\aegis_os\\frontend\\index.html\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🎛️ What Makes This Frontend Exceptional\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  AEGIS // OS  [MISSION CONTROL]  [ZERO-CHAT]              ● SYSTEM ARMED   [▶ RUN DEMO]│\n├──────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┤\n│   1. THE HANDS           │   2. EPISODIC MEMORY        │   3. BOUNDARY HYPERVISOR      │\n│   Virtual OS Desktop     │   Live Canvas Neural Graph  │   Zero-Leak Blast Radius      │\n│  ┌────────────────────┐  │   ┌──────────────────────┐  │   ┌────────────────────────┐  │\n│  │ Legacy ERP v4.2    │  │   │  ● Vendor     ● Inv  │  │   │ Contract: Max $5,000   │  │\n│  │ Smooth Glide Mouse │  │   │      \\       /       │  │   │ Prohibited: Purge/Drop │  │\n│  │ Real-time Typing   │  │   │   \n<truncated 612 bytes>\n────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n#### 1. Simulated Virtual Desktop OS (\"Hands\")\n* A simulated Win32 Legacy Financial ERP with authentic corporate form controls, status bars, and persistent audit ledger.\n* An animated virtual cursor that glides with organic acceleration and deceleration curves (`cubic-bezier`), focuses fields, types values character-by-character, and physically triggers button clicks.\n\n#### 2. Interactive HTML5 Canvas Episodic Memory Graph (\"Memory & Self-Learning\")\n* Real-time particle network rendered on a high-DPI HTML5 canvas showing spatial landmark nodes, coordinate readouts, confidence ratings, and data-flow pulses.\n* **Live Relocalization Animation**: When you click **`[⚡ Trigger Chaos Drift]`**, the ERP button mutates across the screen; the canvas dynamically renders a glowing dashed relocation vector and updates the memory node from `(110, 230)` to `(350, 230) [HEALED]`.\n\n#### 3. Deterministic Boundary Hypervisor & Proof-of-Boundary (\"Boundaries & Trust\")\n* Monitors the active policy invariants ($\\$5,000$ limit, destructive command blocking, atomic snapshotting).\n* When you click **`[💀 Inject Malicious Attack]`** or run Act III, the hypervisor intercepts the action **before the virtual cursor moves**, shifts into an emergency crimson danger state, sounds a warning alarm, and renders a cryptographic **Proof-of-Boundary (PoB)** with SHA-256 hash.\n\n#### 4. Zero-Dependency Web Audio Synthesizer\n* Procedural sound effects using the browser's native Web Audio API (mechanical keystrokes, radar blips, harmonic relocalization chimes, and emergency klaxons) with a quick mute toggle.\n\n---\n\n### 🎬 How to Present It in the Hackathon\n1. Open the frontend in fullscreen in your browser (`F11`).\n2. Click **`[RUN 3-ACT DEMO]`** in the top-right corner.\n3. Deliver your 3-minute pitch while the interface acts out the story in front of the judges!","truncated_fields":["content"]}
