{"step_index":80,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T05:22:04Z","content":"Here is the role distribution for your 5-person team (**2 Frontend + 3 Backend**), structured to avoid merge conflicts and guarantee a 1st-place finish.\n\n---\n\n### 🗺️ Team Matrix at a Glance\n\n| Role | Title | Core Ownership | Hackathon Deliverable |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **FE 1** | **Mission Control & HUD Lead** | UI Architecture, Telemetry, Proof-of-Boundary Cards | Glassmorphic HUD, real-time event logs, judge-facing presentation flow |\n| **FE 2** | **Spatial Canvas & Simulator Specialist** | HTML5 Canvas Graph, Virtual OS Simulator, Web Audio | Neural memory graph animation, cursor physics, Chaos Drift effects |\n| **BE 1** | **Sensory-Motor Engine Lead (\"Hands\")** | OS Actuator, Screen Perception, Multimodal Vision | Mouse gliding, keyboard injection, window capture, Gemini vision hooks |\n| **BE 2** | **Episodic Memory Architect (\"Memory\")** | SQLite State Graph, Drift Detection, Self-Healing | Muscle memory cache, $(\\Delta x, \\Delta y)$ drift calculator, graph re-anchoring |\n| **BE 3** | **Boundary Hypervisor & Security (\"Boundaries\")** | Policy Invariants, Atomic Rollbacks, Target ERP App | Deterministic safety engine, SHA-256 Proof-of-Boundary, mock legacy app |\n\n---\n\n### 👤 Detailed Role Breakdowns\n\n---\n\n#### 🎨 Frontend 1 (FE 1): Mission Control HUD & Experience Lead\n> **Mission:** Make the UI look like a \\$100M Palantir/Vercel enterprise defense console with zero conversational fluff.\n* **Responsibilities:**\n  1. **Top HUD & Layout**: Overall layout, status badges (`SYSTEM ARMED`, `DRIFT HEALING`, `BOUNDARY INTERCEPTED`), and responsive scaling.\n  2. **Audit Telemetry Stream**: The filterable live monospaced terminal showing real-time timestamps, sub-second latency numbers, and invariant passes.\n  3. **Cryptographic Proof-of-Boundary Card**: Design the high-stakes alert card showing the SHA-256 hash, blocked payload summary, and zero-leak confirmation.\n  4. **Pitch Alignment**: Ensure every metric judges care about (perception latency, memory hit rate, blast radius leak = `0.0%`) is pro\n<truncated 4866 bytes>\nodes_cached\": 6,\n    \"drift_detected\": true,\n    \"drift_distance_px\": 240.5\n  },\n  \"hypervisor_disposition\": \"INTERCEPT_BOUNDARY_VIOLATION\",\n  \"proof_of_boundary\": {\n    \"proof_id\": \"POB-9F83A48E\",\n    \"sha256\": \"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae...\",\n    \"violations\": [\"TRANSACTION_CEILING_EXCEEDED: $48,900 > $5,000\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### ⏱️ Hackathon Sync & Milestones (24–36 Hour Schedule)\n\n```mermaid\ngantt\n    title Team Sprint Schedule\n    dateFormat  X\n    axisFormat Hour %H\n\n    section Phase 1: Foundations\n    FE1 (HUD Layout & Telemetry)       :0, 6\n    FE2 (Canvas Graph & OS Viewport)   :0, 6\n    BE1 (Motor Actuator & Perception)  :0, 6\n    BE2 (Episodic SQLite Schema)       :0, 6\n    BE3 (Hypervisor & Mock ERP)        :0, 6\n\n    section Phase 2: Integration\n    BE1 + BE2 (Hands & Memory Loop)    :6, 12\n    BE3 (Hypervisor Intercept & Tests) :6, 12\n    FE1 + FE2 (Canvas & HUD Synthesis) :6, 12\n\n    section Phase 3: The 3-Act Staging\n    All Hands: Act 1 (Hands Actuation) :12, 16\n    All Hands: Act 2 (Chaos Drift)     :16, 20\n    All Hands: Act 3 (Boundary Breach) :20, 24\n\n    section Phase 4: Pitch & Rehearsal\n    Dry-run 3-Minute Demo (10x)        :24, 28\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🎤 Who Does What During the 3-Minute Judge Presentation?\n\n* **Presenter / Storyteller (FE 1 or BE 3)**:\n  * Delivers the speech (*\"We taught rocks to think, and now we use them to write apologies to clients...\"*).\n  * Frames the narrative around the track requirements: Hands, Memory, Boundaries.\n* **Driver / Controller (FE 2 or BE 1)**:\n  * Operates the screen. Hits `[START LIVE 3-ACT DEMO]`, triggers Chaos Mode at the exact right moment, and zooms in on the SHA-256 Proof-of-Boundary.\n* **Q&A Tech Defenders (BE 2, BE 3, BE 1)**:\n  * **BE 2** answers technical questions on drift detection, state graphs, and relocalization algorithms.\n  * **BE 3** answers questions on safety boundaries, deterministic formal verification, and zero-leak rollback guarantees.\n  * **BE 1** explains OS-level event synthesis and coordinate normalization.","thinking":"**Defining Team Roles & Scope**\n\nUnderstand the user's request: assign roles within a 5-person team (2 frontend, 3 backend) for the AegisOS project during a hackathon. The track focuses on AI and Automation. Need to create clear, non-overlapping roles with specific responsibilities. This requires a division of labor that maximizes impact within the hackathon's constraints.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
