{"step_index":96,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T08:49:10Z","thinking":"**Establishing telemetry & HUD updates**\n\nEstablish a WebSocket connection for telemetry data; this is the primary input. Subsequently, define actions based on received messages. On \"MEMORY_DRIFT_DETECTED\", display a HUD alert indicating button relocation, offset by +120px on the x-axis. Further, on \"SELF_HEALING_COMPLETED\", trigger a success card flash and change the relevant node to emerald green. Initial graph nodes must be fetched from a specified endpoint, indicating the application needs to get that data from a GET request.\n\n\n**Implementing WebSocket Status Indicator**\n\nA status indicator will be integrated into the application's header. It will dynamically reflect the WebSocket connection status, providing real-time visual feedback. A fetch call is necessary at initialization for the graph data to be retrieved. This data will be used to initialize the graph representation.\n\n\n**Interpreting Graph Update Function**\n\nThe function `updateGraphFromBE2(data)` must handle data in at least two different formats, either an array or an object. The function's core purpose is to update node positions within the application's local memory and then trigger a UI refresh to reflect these changes. Both formats must be handled gracefully.\n\n\n**Defining WebSocket error handling**\n\nWebSocket error handling is defined with specific visual cues.  A failed connection sets the status to \"ERR\" with a rose-colored indicator. Closed connections trigger a reconnection attempt with an amber status, and automatic reconnect every 3 seconds. Failed initialization attempts retry after 5 seconds.\n\n**Implementing memory drift detection**\n\nA drift event handler is implemented, triggered by data events labeled `\"MEMORY_DRIFT_DETECTED\"`. The alert displays a HUD warning with the button's relocation, defaulting to +120px on the x-axis if not specified. An alert banner will also be updated with the specific error message.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Piyush\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\aegis_os\\\\frontend\\\\index.html\"","ContentOffset":"0","EndLine":"150","StartLine":"125","toolAction":"\"Viewing header actions\"","toolSummary":"\"View header action buttons in frontend/index.html\""}}]}
