pdating Memory Graph Node Data**\n\nThe incoming data structure necessitates a check to see if the nodes already exist in memory. Nodes are updated with new values for `x`, `y`, and `label` if they a\n<truncated 1318 bytes>\nme from various potential fields (`event`, `type`, etc.).  It specifically looks for \"MEMORY_DRIFT_DETECTED\" and \"SELF_HEALING_COMPLETED\" events. Any other messages are logged.\n\n**Implementing Memory Drift Alert**\n\nWhen a \"MEMORY_DRIFT_DETECTED\" event is detected, a function is invoked to trigger a visual alert. The `deltaX` value, either specified in the data or defaulted to 120, will be passed to this function.\n\n**Handling Self-Healing Completion**\n\nOn the detection of the \"SELF_HEALING_COMPLETED\" event, a separate handler function is called. The data associated with this event will be used by the called function, but the specific process is not within the scope of this code snippet.\n\n\n**Responding to Memory Drift Detected**\n\nA \"MEMORY_DRIFT_DETECTED\" event triggers a multi-stage response. First, visual alerts are displayed via a HUD card and a bottom banner, informing the user about the button's relocation delta. Subsequently, the target button in the ERP view is repositioned by the detected delta, with visual feedback. The system status badge is updated to reflect the drift and the ongoing relocalization. Finally, a relocalization vector animation is initiated on the canvas, visually representing the shift.\n\n\n**Analyzing Self-Healing Completion**\n\nThe function `triggerSelfHealingCompleted` handles the visual feedback for a successful self-healing event. This includes hiding drift alerts, displaying a success card on the HUD, and triggering a central column toast. The success card fades out after a short duration.\n\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\n**Visualizing Self-Healing Success**\n\nA toast notification animates in, indicating the self-healing completion. Subsequently, the \"submit\" node's visual state changes: its color becomes emerald green, and its pulse effect is activated.\n\nThe table data reflecting the \"submit\" node is updated to reflect its \"HEALED\" status and the normalized coordinates are updated.  The HUD status and relevant metrics are updated to reflect the successful healing event.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"@'\\nimport re\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nfiles = [\\n    Path(r\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Piyush\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\aegis_os\\\\frontend\\\\index.html\\\"),\\n    Path(r\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Piyush\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\e426a91e-3961-4012-84ca-1849c4385ef7\\\\aegis_mission_control.html\\\")\\n]\\n\\nws_badge_html = '''\\n      <!-- BE2 Live Wi-Fi Server Status Badge -->\\n      <div id=\\\"ws-status-badge\\\" class=\\\"px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-slate-900 border border-slate-700 text-slate-300 flex items-center space-x-2 font-mono text-[11px] transition-all\\\">\\n        <span id=\\\"ws-indicator-dot\\\" class=\\\"w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-amber-400 animate-ping\\\"></span>\\n        <span id=\\\"ws-status-text\\\">WS: CONNECTING (172.18.238.74)</span>\\n      </div>\\n'''\\n\\nalert_cards_html = '''\\n    <!-- BE2 LIVE TELEMETRY WARNING ALERT CARD -->\\n    <div id=\\\"be2-drift-alert\\\" class=\\\"fixed top-16 left-1/2 transform -translate-x-1/2 z-50 w-full max-w-xl p-3.5 rounded-xl bg-amber-950/95 border-2 border-amber-500 text-amber-100 font-mono text-xs shadow-[0_0_30px_rgba(245,158,11,0.35)] -translate-y-24 opacity-0 transition-all duration-300 flex items-center justify-between pointer-events-none\\\">\\n      <div class=\\\"flex items-center space-x-3\\\">\\n        <span class=\\\"w-3.5 h-3.5 rounded-full bg-amber-400 animate-ping\\\"></span>\\n        <div>\\n          <div class=\\\"font-extrabold text-amber-300 text-xs tracking-wider uppercase\\\">⚠ MEMORY DRIFT DETECTED [BE2 TELEMETRY]</div>\\n          <div id=\\\"be2-drift-msg\\\" class=\\\"text-[1